speechtext:
That a sum not exceeding $10,502,377,163.36 being composed of:
(1)	three-twelfths ($7,285,634,730.00) of the total amounts of the items set forth in the Main Estimates for the fiscal year ending March 31, 1986, which were laid upon the Table on Tuesday, February 26, 1985; except those items detailed below:
(2)	eleven-twelfths of the total amount of Energy, Mines and Resources Item 20, Public Works Items 40 and 45, Transport Item 25 and Treasury Board Item 10 (Schedule A) of the said Estimates $55,440,000.00;
(3)	nine-twelfths of the total amounts of Solicitor General Item 5, and Treasury Board Item 5 (Schedule B) in said Estimates $377,933,250.00;
(4)	eight-twelfths of the total amount of Indian Affairs and Northern Development Item 50 (Schedule C) of the said Estimates $10,906,666.67;
(5)	seven-twelfths of the total amounts of Employment and Immigration Item 15 (Schedule D) of the said Estimates, $387,307,083.33;
(6)	six-twelfths of the total amounts of Transport Items 35, L45 and L50 (Schedule E) of the said Estimates, $14,590,000.00;
(7)	five-twelfths of the total amounts of Communications Items 5 and 50, Consumer and Corporate Affairs Item 15, Indian Affairs and Northern Development Item 15, National Health and Welfare Item 55 and Veterans Affairs Item 15 (Schedule F) of the said Estimates $518,772,500.01; and
(8)	four-twelfths of the total amounts of Communications Item 35, Consumer and Corporate Affairs Item 10, Employment and Immigration Items I, 5, 10 and 25, Energy, Mines and Resources Items I and 45, External Affairs Item 45, Finance Item 25, Indian Affairs and Northern Development Items 30, 35 and 40, National Health and Welfare Item 10, Public Works Items 10 and 50, Secretary of State Items 25 and 45, Supply and Services Item 15, Transport Items 55 and 85, and Veterans Affairs Items 20, 25 and 30 (Schedule G) of the said Estimates, $1,851,792,933.35;
be granted to Her Majesty on account of the fiscal year ending March 31, 1986.
